      "side": 1,
      "message": "`HW_TEST` is a user configurable config to include hardware tests. It is \u003dy in RO/RW, even if `HW_TEST_RW_ONLY\u003dy`. `HW_TEST_ON` is a helper config, noT-user configurable, that is \u003dy only in RW if `HW_TEST_RW_ONLY\u003dy`. It is used in CMakeFile\n`add_subdirectory_ifdef(CONFIG_HW_TEST_ON \"test/hwtest\")` and to include Kconfig file to avoid complicated if statements like\n```\nif HW_TEST \u0026\u0026 ((HW_TEST_RW_ONLY \u0026\u0026 CROS_EC_RW) || (!HW_TEST_RW_ONLY))\n...\n```\n\n(1) I\u0027m ready to do some adjustment if needed.\n\n(2) I\u0027m always building `main.c` if `HW_TEST\u003dy`, because `ec_app_main` has to be called in every cases anyway. Then I\u0027m using `ZTEST_SHELL` config to determine if tests should be run automatically or not. I don\u0027t know how it is done with gTest.\nDo you think another config `HW_TEST_MAIN` is really needed, or you are think `HW_TEST` is not necessary? There has to be any config to add CMake subdirectory or gate building test main.",
